      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Obesity involves hypoxic adipose tissue and low-grade chronic inflammation. We investigated the impact of hypoxia on inflammatory response to TNF-α in white and brown adipocytes. In response to TNF-α, the expression of the inducible enzymes iNOS and COX-2 was prominently and selectively potentiated during hypoxia while only moderately under normoxia. Levels of their products, nitrite and prostaglandinE2 were elevated accordingly. NS398, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, reduced nitrite levels. The expression of PGC-1α, a transcriptional co-activator involved in mitochondrial biogenesis, and PPARγ, a transcription factor involved in adipocyte homeostasis, was reduced by TNF-α during hypoxia. These results suggest that hypoxia potentiates the inflammatory response by TNF-α in both white and brown adipocytes and downregulates the transcription factors involved in adipocyte function."
      },
